# Vendored library provenance (R2 fallback - see docs/dependency-strategy.md).
#
# The external-source pin (fkst.workspace.toml [[external_sources]] + fkst.lock)
# was REJECTED by the engine: the real `workflow` library is publishable = false,
# and add_external_units only admits publishable libraries across an external-source
# boundary (it lands in denied_external_libraries otherwise). fkst-packages is
# read/pin/vendor-only, so the publishable flag cannot be changed at the source.
# Fallback: vendor the minimal required library with a REAL manifest.
#
# source_repo  = ChronoAIProject/fkst-packages (local: marketing-tbd/fkst-packages)
# source_sha   = 8704a642f9c61023a2bbb50fade0c24483680eeb
# source_path  = libraries/workflow/saga.lua
# vendored     = saga.lua (verbatim, byte-identical to source @ source_sha)
#
# Only saga.lua is vendored: persistence_class="saga" requires
# require("workflow.saga").department, and saga.lua has zero external requires
# (no contract dependency), so this is the minimal conformant subset. The full
# upstream workflow library (codex/oracle/sweep/dead_letter/liveness/...) and its
# `contract` transitive dep are intentionally NOT vendored.
#
# To refresh: re-copy libraries/workflow/saga.lua from the source repo at the
# pinned SHA (or a newer reviewed SHA) and update source_sha above.
